This script configures BGP to advertise and connect pod networks in different
ways.

The enviroment is assumed to be a dev-scripts setup or equivalent, where this
script runs on the hypervisor.

This script:

* runs an FRR container representing a router/spine external BGP peer
* for every advertised network configuration, an external agnhost container is
  created connected exclusively to that network through the FRR container in
  that configuration 
* advertises the default pod network over the default VRF
* advertises [every network][1] defined in EXTRA_NETWORKS dev-scripts
  variable in a VRF-Lite configuration
* advertises networks [labeled with `macvrf=true`][2] in a [EVPN MACVRF][3] configuration
* advertises network [labeled with `ipvrf=true`][2] in a [EVPN IPVRF][3] configuration

For EVPN networks, the script can stub the OCP EVPN implementation if
`EVPN_IMPLEMENTED` nevironment variable is set to 0

See 

[1]: TODO: only supports one network
[2]: L2 networks can labeled both ways at the same time, L3 networks only with
     `ipvrf=true`. Network also needs to be labeled with `network=<network name>`
[3]: TODO: only IPv4 supported

